                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.37219/2610.37219v1/fig_designspace_ppt.png",
                "caption": "Figure 1:The three choices that separate VLAs, WAMs, and JAM: backbone initialization, the objective on recorded future observations, and the modules kept at inference. (a) The VLA reference uses no future objective, only the action lossℒact\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{act}}. (b) WAMs add visual generation lossℒG\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{G}}. The dashed loop shows generated future observations entering the action expert in some WAMs. (c) JAM uses foresight lossℒF\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{F}}across pretraining families, discards its supervision branch, and retains the corresponding action path.",
                "position": 321
            }
        ]
